# Cursor Rules — Shared Knowledge Repository

This file is a thin alias. The **binding rules** live in [AI_GUIDELINES.md](AI_GUIDELINES.md).
Cursor must follow the entirety of the rules defined there.

## Context

This is a knowledge-management repository for AI agents. It contains skills, agents, patterns, decisions, and domain notes extracted from real projects. It is **not** an application — it is a structured documentation knowledge base organized by **domain-first taxonomy** (`llm/`, `sfad/`, …).

## Cursor-specific notes

- Reply language: match the user (Italian or English). All generated repository content: English.
- Code, identifiers, file names, commit messages: English.
- Prefer multi-edit operations when changing multiple sections of the same file.
- Always read [AI_GUIDELINES.md](AI_GUIDELINES.md) and [MAP.md](MAP.md) before suggesting changes to the catalog.
- Do not suggest source code — this repository contains Markdown documentation only.
- Before creating a new file, check for affinity with existing files in the same domain folder.
- An agent requires ≥ 2 included skills; never create an agent with one skill.

## Read first

1. [AI_GUIDELINES.md](AI_GUIDELINES.md) — master rules.
2. [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) — supported commands and processing behavior.
3. [MAP.md](MAP.md) — current skills/agents/knowledge per domain.
4. [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) — contribution workflow for humans and agents.
